WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.657
Welcome to Section Three: Organizing.

2
00:00:02.857 --> 00:00:05.324
A plan identifies the result we want.

3
00:00:05.524 --> 00:00:09.101
Organizing arranges the work and people needed to
achieve it.

4
00:00:09.301 --> 00:00:14.750
At our fictional Cedar Crossing Library, a flexible
learning room now hosts community workshops.

5
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.861
Programs staff arrange speakers.

6
00:00:17.061 --> 00:00:19.864
Public services staff welcome participants.

7
00:00:20.064 --> 00:00:22.103
Technical support prepares equipment.

8
00:00:22.303 --> 00:00:27.616
But two announcements give different times, and everyone
assumes someone else has checked the materials.

9
00:00:27.816 --> 00:00:31.571
The problem may be the connections between jobs, not a
lack of effort.

10
00:00:31.771 --> 00:00:40.318
Our route moves from service purpose to work and
dependencies, roles and authority, coordination and
culture, then review and adaptation.

11
00:00:40.518 --> 00:00:43.514
Every Cedar Crossing event and outcome is invented.

12
00:00:43.714 --> 00:00:46.886
This optional lesson supports Chapters Seven through
Nine.

13
00:00:47.086 --> 00:00:51.083
You still need the readings and your own analysis of
“Differential Treatment?”

14
00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:55.218
Listen, read, revisit, or skip an activity whenever you
choose.

